# Project Statement

## Project Title
Student To-Do List Manager

## Problem Statement
Students manage assignments, personal activities, projects and deadlines across notebooks or different applications. This can make it difficult to see what is pending, what is completed, and which tasks are urgent. The proposed application provides a centralized To-Do List Manager.

## Proposed Solution
A Python desktop application allows users to create, organize, search, filter, complete and delete tasks. Data is stored locally in JSON format so tasks remain available after restarting the application.

## Target Users
Students and individual users who need a simple personal task-management system.

## Core Modules
1. Task Management
2. Validation
3. Persistent Storage
4. Search and Filtering
5. Analytics
6. Graphical User Interface

## Inputs
Task title, description, due date, priority, category and task actions.

## Outputs
Task table, filtering results, completion status and progress statistics.

## Scope
The application is intended as a lightweight single-user desktop productivity tool.

## Limitations
The current version does not provide online accounts, multi-user collaboration, cloud synchronization or push notifications.
